A||||11||Scott_M||Alternator..replace or refurbish????||||1||
Z||000000||Scott_M||06-27-2000||04:08 PM||||I have an manual 87 SE at 113k mi, with an alternator that isn't putting out enough juice. Is it more economical to buy a replacement($75) or take it in for fixing($$$)? Any opinions would be appreciated. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-27-2000||04:20 PM||||I usually replace them. <P>It depends on who you have around to rebuild them. If they do a good job it's great, if they skimp you end up with crap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ROB MAC||06-27-2000||07:40 PM||||Either way your getting a rebuilt unit and it costs about the same.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||06-27-2000||09:48 PM||||If you can find a rebuilt unit that has had everything replaced,then you're better off than the funky ones that only replace what was totally smoked,and leave the rest to test.I hate it when I go to look at the rebuilt alternator,and it's bearings are more sloppy,or obviously binding than the old one that only needed a set of brushes.<BR>You might try a Delco brand rebuild.<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||06-27-2000||09:48 PM||||If you can find a rebuilt unit that has had everything replaced,then you're better off than the funky ones that only replace what was totally smoked,and leave the rest to test.I hate it when I go to look at the rebuilt alternator,and it's bearings are more sloppy,or obviously binding than the old one that only needed a set of brushes.<BR>You might try a Delco,or Bosch brand rebuild.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||06-28-2000||11:41 PM||||alternators generally take a beating in Fiero with all the engine heat. My solution was Autozone Gold series rebuilt lifetime warranty. $60 and they give me a brand new one everytime it cooks. (about every 1 1/2 years) Im an expert now and can change one over in about 15 minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000006||chris6878||06-29-2000||02:45 AM||||my dad had one rebuilt the other day (87 buick 4cyl) for $40  at the local starter shop. The alternator he needed for his car cost $90. So he saved $ big time and the alternator works fine. I would call around and see...<P>Just my opinion...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>later,<BR>chris||||reg||3
Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||06-29-2000||07:23 AM||||$20 at your local junk yard. Just pop them open and make sure the windings are fried and theres no burn marks on it, oh and check the bearings too. Of course you wave the warenty, and you have no garuntee it'll work, but it's only $20. it's better to go with a new one, or a refurb w/ a warenty, but if you just need something to get you to work and back until payday...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroSTETZ||06-30-2000||02:14 AM||||try checking kragen, i bought an alternator there for 100 bucks, it came with a lifetime guarantee- its also not bs because I asked the guy how limited it was and he said its actually a good deal (neighbor of mine) does the fiero seem to use an especially "beefy" alternator for its size or what? the one in my car is 105.. that seems huge compared to the one on my mazda- 60 amps||||reg||1
Z||000009||shain||07-01-2000||07:57 AM||||you can buy a rebuild kit for 15 bucks and do it your self! if your a handy guy. the alt ihad be 4 was 72 amps then (stupid me) i got one from a scrap yard and it was a 66 amp and it sucked! it would cause my engine to idle high and low rapidly.<P>IF YOU HAVE A FOUR BANGER 105 AMPS IS A LOT!!  I DONT KNOW IF THAT IS GOOD.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BN Boomer||07-01-2000||10:14 AM||||Hey Scott, I have an alternator off of an 87 4 cylinder that you can have for the cost of shipping if you want. It worked fine when I pulled it out a year ago. If you'd like, I'll even take it down to the local auto supply store and have it tested to make sure it's still in good working order. Let me know if you're intersted....||||reg||1
Z||000011||Scott_M||07-02-2000||01:10 AM||||Thanks boomer but I endewd up buying a rebuilt one the other day from autozone for $75. I appreciate the thought though.||||reg||1
